WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.410
Monitoring understanding means checking comprehension while reading, listening,

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.840
practicing, or solving a problem.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.040
Instead of waiting until the end to discover that the thread was lost,

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.880
you notice confusion as it appears.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.720
You pay attention to moments when the details stop connecting, when a term is unclear,

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.315
when an assumption slips in unnoticed, or when progress is only superficial.

00:00:18.315 --> 00:00:22.030
This skill is especially important in complex work because errors can compound.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:25.600
A small misunderstanding in the first step can shape every decision that follows.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.330
In troubleshooting, a weak assumption can cause a person to collect the wrong evidence.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.770
In writing, an unclear claim can make the rest of the argument unstable.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.760
Monitoring lets you adjust before the cost of correction grows.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.280
Good monitoring uses questions.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.550
What do I think this means?

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.640
What evidence supports that interpretation?

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.120
Which part is still uncertain?

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.275
What assumption am I making?

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:45.455
Could I explain the last step without looking?

00:00:45.455 --> 00:00:47.200
What would I need to see to change my mind?

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.420
These questions slow the work just enough to keep it aligned with reality.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.080
Monitoring does not mean stopping every few seconds.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.620
It means creating checkpoints at meaningful moments.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.640
Pause after a section, a decision, a failed attempt, or a new piece of evidence.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.760
If the material still makes sense, continue.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.320
If it does not, change the strategy: reread, draw a diagram, ask a better question,

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.275
test the assumption, or seek review before errors harden.

00:01:09.275 --> 00:01:11.480
A useful signal is the phrase, I sort of get it.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.370
That may be true, but it deserves testing.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:16.720
Sort of understanding is often enough to follow someone else's explanation,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.480
but not enough to act independently.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.405
When that feeling appears, convert it into a concrete check: summarize the idea,

00:01:22.405 --> 00:01:25.920
apply it to a small case, or name the part that is still unclear.
